{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":303769,"duration_api_ms":302555,"num_turns":39,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"8f635772-626b-49fc-a03d-d11da88ea97f","total_cost_usd":1.5926102500000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":25,"cache_creation_input_tokens":87253,"cache_read_input_tokens":1565558,"output_tokens":10575,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":87253,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":25,"outputTokens":10575,"cacheReadInputTokens":1565558,"cacheCreationInputTokens":87253,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.5926102500000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Thorough review of the concentration helper API implementation (tanksim-6e5.2.2). The changeset introduces canonical concentration helpers on WaterState/TankState/ConcentrationView, a legacy parameter bridge via LEGACY_KINETIC_REFERENCE_VOLUME_L, substrate-aware net water volume, schema v2→v3 migration, and comprehensive test coverage including property tests. All 80+ tests pass, clippy is clean. The implementation is well-structured: concentration_from_total guards against zero/NaN volume, all system files consistently use state.water_volume_l() instead of state.geometry.water_volume_l(), the Monod kinetics correctly switch from total-based to concentration-based terms, and the save migration correctly preserves concentrations when rescaling totals. The ConcentrationView pattern cleanly avoids recomputing volume on each accessor call. Two minor concerns flagged below; no bugs or safety issues found.","amendments":[{"body":"In `tank_tui/src/main.rs:597`, the scenario selection screen displays \"Filled volume\" using `geometry.water_volume_l()` (gross volume without substrate displacement). Now that all chemistry uses net water volume via `state.water_volume_l()`, this display is inconsistent with the concentration math. Consider either (a) showing both gross and net volumes, or (b) labeling this as \"Tank capacity\" to distinguish it from actual water volume.","rationale":"Users who compare the displayed volume against concentration back-calculations (total / displayed_volume) will get wrong answers. This is a UX correctness gap, not a simulation bug, but it undermines trust in the numbers."},{"body":"The `LEGACY_KINETIC_REFERENCE_VOLUME_L = 20.0` constant in process.rs derives from the default tank's net water volume (40×25×22/1000 − 40×25×2/1000 = 20 L). Add a one-line doc comment noting this derivation so a future change to default TankGeometry or default substrate depth doesn't silently break the legacy parameter bridge.","rationale":"If someone changes the default geometry dimensions or default substrate depth in the future, the reference constant would become stale relative to the default tank, breaking the calibration assumption without any compiler error or test failure. A doc comment ties these together."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"4fbb6fbf-c3be-4214-bbdf-93fa6a58147e"}
